				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2902864&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607460152" alt="MaliceAforethought" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2902864)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;" >MaliceAforethought</a></span> <span class="odate time_1511999277 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Nov 2017 23:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3642475">
									

<p>Alright, that title was dumb. Apologies.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>manufactured by &quot;KIPPER MEDIA, INC.&quot; sometime in the 1980s.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;sometime&quot; sounds very slightly informal here. But hey, that's just personal preference.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3139-1-A will stalk and pursue the camera operator</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How can you stalk someone <em>without</em> pursuing them? I get what you mean, but it seems a little redundant. &quot;Stalk&quot;, also sounds a tad to un-clinical for an SCP document.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Object Class: Euclid</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Un-bolden that &quot;Euclid&quot; soldier!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(see Addendum II for further information on the latter).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The redaction almost turned me off the article, but the fact that you clarified it shows a fairly good grasp of how people on the site think :P<br />
&quot;Further information&quot; is inaccurate though &#8212; you don't give <em>any</em> information to begin with.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3139-1 is subject to the laws of time and exists as a separate reality from our own.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>But -1 is the contents of a tape. Do you mean something along the lines of 'the area depicted in SCP-3139-1'?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Viewer's biological child (before and after their birth)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Something about this sentence gets me in all the wrong ways. Well done.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>our lucky contestant was…less than lucky</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Space after ellipse.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Host: We claim another. We claim another. Glorious prey. Your [inaudible] are delicious. Delicious. [audience laughter]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Oh my god.</p>
<p>This is reminiscent of Laugh Is Fun, but less surreal and more thought provoking. It doesn't have the wacky charm of Laugh, but it plays on the same tropes in a different way, taking a straight path to horror instead of meandering weirdness. I felt the recording could have gone on longer and provided a little more in the way of atmosphere, but the real-world consequences combined with the effective imagery comes together to make this surprisingly horrifying for a people-stealing game show. You've clearly put effort in with regards to pacing and structure, and it's payed off in spades.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Easy +1, and I hope to see more of this stuff in the future :D</p>

							</div>

								
					
